      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A railroad spur from Riverside turned Hemet into a trading hub for citrus, apricots, peaches, olives, and walnuts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemet%2C_California",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Historic Hemet Theater, built in 1921, once held the title of the nation’s oldest continually running single‑screen theater.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
